        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "An Illinois **LCPC** license expires **March 31 of odd-numbered years**.\n\n* Illinois Administrative Code, Title 68, Part 1375 — **PROFESSIONAL COUNSELOR AND CLINICAL PROFESSIONAL COUNSELOR LICENSING ACT** — provides in Section 1375.200 Renewals:\n\n> Every license issued under the Act shall expire on March 31 of odd numbered years.\n\n* IDFPR states the same rule:\n\n> All Professional Counselor licenses expire March 31 of odd years.\n\nThe first licensure period may be less than 2 years. After the first renewal, the licensure cycle is 2 years.\n\nThe holder may renew the license preceding the expiration date at a time determined by the Division by paying the fee set forth in Section 1375.205 and completing 30 hours of continuing education in accordance with Section 1375.220.",
          "annotations": [
            {
              "type": "url_citation",
              "url": "https://www.ilga.gov/commission/Jcar/admincode/068/068013750C02000R.html",
